{"type":"message","id":"134e4ffb","parentId":"7068aaf8","timestamp":"2026-06-28T12:48:49.682Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So the working tree is clean — the commit already went through with the changes that were staged. But the commit message mentioned \"5+ new airframe candidates\" which doesn't seem accurate based on the diff I saw (it only shows the manufacturerFlightTime attributes being added, not new candidates). Let me look more carefully at what was added...\n\nActually, I looked at the diff vs HEAD~1, and that diff shows only the `manufacturerFlightTime` being added to existing entries. But maybe the \"5+ new\" were already in the file before my commit and came from David's earlier work. Let me check by searching for airframe candidates that appear in the file but were not in the previous commit.\n\nWait - David said \"Please make sure that the candidates.sysml is updated to add these 5 new options.\" So he's saying those 5 new options weren't added. Let me check what was in the file before my commit vs after my commit more carefully.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_details"},{"type":"text","text":"David — it sounds like the \"5+ new airframe candidates\" I mentioned in the commit message may not have actually been added. Let me check whether they were already present or are still missing"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_c8def839a677464e84d88660","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone && git diff HEAD~1 -- candidates.sysml | grep -E '^\\+' | head -60"},"partialArgs":"{\"command\": \"cd /home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone && git diff HEAD~1 -- candidates.sysml | grep -E '^\\\\+' | head -60\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":111,"output":326,"cacheRead":63488,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoningTokens":200,"totalTokens":63925,"cost":{"input":0.0000110999999999