{"type":"message","id":"03144eab","parentId":"1f43ee24","timestamp":"2026-06-28T12:49:02.450Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Looking at the diff carefully, the last commit (0cbb77f) only added `manufacturerFlightTime` and `manufacturerFlightTimeBattery` attributes to the existing airframe entries. It did NOT add any new airframe candidates beyond what was already in the file.\n\nLet me count the airframe parts currently in the file:\n1. AF1a - GEPRC MOZ7 V2 Analog\n2. AF1b - GEPRC MOZ7 V2 WTFPV\n3. AF1c - GEPRC MOZ7 V2 O4 Pro\n4. AF2b - Axisflying KOLAS7 BNF Analog\n5. AF2c - Axisflying KOLAS7 BNF HD\n6. AF3a - iFlight Chimera9 ECO PNP\n7. AF3b - iFlight Chimera9 ECO BNF\n8. AF4a - DarwinFPV X9 PNP\n9. AF5 - EMAX Hawk 7 BNF\n10. AF6a - DeepSpace ROC7 O4 PRO PNP\n11. AF6b - DeepSpace ROC7 O4 PRO BNF\n12. AF7 - GEPRC Crocodile75 V3 PNP\n13. AF8a - iFlight Chimera7 Pro V2 PNP\n14. AF8b - iFlight Chimera7 Pro V2 BNF\n15. AF9a - DarwinFPV 129 7in PNP\n16. AF10 - NewBeeDrone ROC7 O4PRO BNF\n\nSo those are the existing candidates. The commit message was wrong — it said \"Add 5+ new candidate airframes\" but actually only added flight time data to existing ones. David is now asking me to make sure the 5 new options are actually added.\n\nLet me re-read what David said: \"Please make sure that the candidates.sysml is updated to add these 5 new options.\"\n\nSo I need to figure out what 5 new options he's referring to. Let me search memory for any discussion about new airframe candidates.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_details"},{"type":"text","text":"I see the issue — my commit message was wrong. The last commit **only added flight time attributes** to existing candidates, not the 5 new airframe options. Let me check what's been discussed about new candidates"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_002af68a1a924387ab24211a","name":"memory_search","arguments":{"query":"new airframe candidates 5 options candidates.sysml"},"partialArgs":"{\"qu