{"type":"message","id":"bf00bbe3","parentId":"bd081ecf","timestamp":"2026-06-28T12:49:18.363Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Memory search is down, but looking at the evidence:\n\n1. The commit `0cbb77f` only added `manufacturerFlightTime` and `manufacturerFlightTimeBattery` attributes to the existing candidates (AF1a through AF10). No new airframe parts were added.\n2. The commit message was misleading — it said \"Add 5+ new airframe candidates\" but actually didn't add any new candidates.\n\nThe current `candidates.sysml` already has quite a few candidates (AF1a through AF10), which includes the recent MOZ7 V2 variants and the ROC7 variants. \n\nBut David is asking me to make sure the candidates.sysml is updated to add these 5 new options. I need to figure out what \"these 5 new options\" refers to. Looking at the file, the existing airframe candidates are:\n- AF1a-c: GEPRC MOZ7 V2 (Analog, WTFPV, O4 Pro) - 3 variants\n- AF2b-c: Axisflying KOLAS7 (BNF Analog, BNF HD) - 2 variants \n- AF3a-b: iFlight Chimera9 ECO (PNP, BNF) - 2 variants\n- AF4a: DarwinFPV X9 - 1 variant\n- AF5: EMAX Hawk 7 - 1 variant\n- AF6a-b: DeepSpace ROC7 O4 PRO (PNP+GPS, BNF) - 2 variants\n- AF7: GEPRC Crocodile75 V3 - 1 variant\n- AF8a-b: iFlight Chimera7 Pro V2 (PNP, BNF) - 2 variants\n- AF9a: DarwinFPV 129 7in - 1 variant\n- AF10: NewBeeDrone ROC7 O4PRO - 1 variant\n\nWait, AF10 is already there! So are the 5 new options I need to add something else?\n\nLet me re-read David's message: \"Oh. Please make sure that the candidates.sysml is updated to add these 5 new options.\"\n\nThis sounds like he thinks there should be 5 new airframe candidates added that weren't in my commit. Since the commit didn't actually add any new candidates (just flight time attributes), he's likely referring to candidates that should be there.\n\nLooking at what's already in the file, there are already quite a few. Maybe the new candidates are something specific he mentioned earlier but hasn't seen added yet. Since I can't search memory, let me check what recent changes look like and if there are notes about what new candidates are being added.\n\nActually, let me re-read his message more carefully. He said \"Please make sure that the candidates.sysml is updated to add these 5 new options\" - meaning after my initial commit + push, he's asking me to verify that the 5 new airframe candidates are actually in there. Since they weren't part of the commit at all, they're not in there.\n\nBut I don't actually know what specific 5 new airframes he's referring to. Let me look at this from a different angle - what airframes might be missing or what did I previously discuss adding?\n\nLooking at the file structure, there are gaps in the numbering (AF9a has only one variant, AF10 exists). The file already has multiple airframes from HGLRC, DarwinFPV, DeepSpace, GEPRC, NewBeeDrone...\n\nWait - I think my commit message literally referred to \"5+ new candidates\" from \"HGLRC, DarwinFPV, DeepSpace, GEPRC, NewBeeDrone, and others\". But looking at the file, most of these are already there:\n- GEPRC: MOZ7 V2 variants, Crocodile75\n- DarwinFPV: X9, 129 7in\n- DeepSpace: ROC7\n- NewBeeDrone: ROC7\n\nHGLRC isn't represented! That might be one of the missing ones.\n\nActually, I think the most reasonable interpretation is: the commit I made didn't actually add the new candidates it said it did, and David is asking me to actually add them. But I need to know WHICH 5 new candidates he means.\n\nLet me just be honest with David and ask which specific new options he's referring to, while acknowledging that my previous commit was incorrectly described.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_details"},{"type":"text","text":"You're right — my commit message was wrong. That commit only added `manufacturerFlightTime` attributes to **existing** candidates, not the 5 new options. The file is unchanged from before.\n\nCould you point me to which 5 new airframe candidates you want added? I see we've already got:\n\n- **GEPRC** — MOZ7 V2 (3 variants), Crocodile75\n- **iFlight** — Chimera9 ECO (2), Chimera7 Pro V2 (2)\n- **Axisflying** — KOLAS7 (2)\n- **DarwinFPV** — X9, 129 7in\n- **DeepSpace / NewBeeDrone** — ROC7 O4PRO (3 variants total)\n- **EMAX** — Hawk 7\n\nWant me to add some HGLRC models, or specific other 7-9\" LR airframes I should source? Let me know which ones and I'll get them drafted and committed."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":47408,"output":1136,"cacheRead":17280,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoningTokens":927,"totalTokens":65824,"cost":{"input":0.0047408,"output":0.0002272,"cacheRead":0.0003456,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0053136}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1782650942543,"responseId":"gen-1782650943-RkqiKkowAd1MRaYWRPMg"}}
{"type":"message","id":"875c4394-f12e-481e-9e39-8a5799c1508c","parentId":"bf00bbe3","timestamp":"2026-06-28T12:49:20.652Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You're right — my commit message was wrong. That commit only added `manufacturerFlightTime` attributes to **existing** candidates, not the 5 new options. The file is unchanged from before.\n\nCould you point me to which 5 new airframe candidates you want added? I see we've already got:\n\n- **GEPRC** — MOZ7 V2 (3 variants), Crocodile75\n- **iFlight** — Chimera9 ECO (2), Chimera7 Pro V2 (2)\n- **Axisflying** — KOLAS7 (2)\n- **DarwinFPV** — X9, 129 7in\n- **DeepSpace / NewBeeDrone** — ROC7 O4PRO (3 variants total)\n- **EMAX** — Hawk 7\n\nWant me to add some HGLRC models, or specific other 7-9\" LR airframes I should source? Let me know which ones and I'll get them drafted and committed."}],"api":"openai-responses","provider":"openclaw","model":"delivery-mirror","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"total":0,"prompt_tokens":0,"completion_tokens":0,"total_tokens":0,"cache":{"read":0,"write":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1782650960643}}
{"type":"message","id":"0da6cd8c","parentId":"875c4394-f12e-481e-9e39-8a5799c1508c","timestamp":"2026-06-28T12:49:53.510Z","message":{"role":"user","content":"Now I have enough data. Here's what I found across manufacturers and retailers:\n\n───\n\n5+ New Airframe Candidates (7-9\" BNF/PNP)\n\n**1. HGLRC Rekon7 PRO** (7\")\n\n• **URL:** [https://www.hglrc.com/products/rekon7-pro-long-range-fpv-analog-digital-version-racing-drone](https://www.hglrc.com/products/rekon7-pro-long-range-fpv-analog-digital-version-racing-drone)\n• **Price:** ~$549.99 (BNF, analog); ~$599 (HD)\n• **Mass:** 576g (DJI O3 version)\n• **Wheelbase:** 324mm\n• **Motors:** SPECTER 2806.5 1350KV\n• **FC:** SPECTER F405 V2 / **ESC:** SPECTER 60A BL_S\n• **Flight Time:** ~20-25 min (Alibaba listing) — no manufacturer claim\n• **Battery:** LiPo 6S 3000mAh / VTC6 2P 4000mAh\n• **Prop:** 7\" HQProp DP7X4X3\n• **GPS:** M80 PRO (pre-installed)\n• **Key differentiator:** Lightest weight of any candidate under 600g, dedicated long-range build by Dave C / HGLRC\n\n**2. iFlight SH CineLR 7** (7.5\")\n\n• **URL:** [https://pyrodrone.com/products/iflight-sh-cinelr-7-o4-6s-hd-long-range-bnf-w-dji-o4-air-unit-pro-choose-receiver](https://pyrodrone.com/products/iflight-sh-cinelr-7-o4-6s-hd-long-range-bnf-w-dji-o4-air-unit-pro-choose-receiver)\n• **Price:** $1,019.99 (BNF w/ DJI O4 Pro)\n• **Mass:** 770g\n• **Wheelbase:** 334mm\n• **Motors:** XING2 2809 1250KV\n• **FC:** BLITZ F722 / **ESC:** BLITZ E55 55A\n• **Flight Time:** ~25 min with 6S 8000mAh Li-ion\n• **Prop:** HQ 7.5x3.7x3\n• **Key differentiator:** No props in view frame design — clean thermal camera FOV\n\n**3. iFlight Chimera7 Eco** (7.5\") — _budget pick_\n\n• **URL:** [https://pyrodrone.com/products/iflight-chimera7-eco-analog-5-8g-1-6w-vtx-6s-long-range-bnf-elrs-2-4ghz-rx](https://pyrodrone.com/products/iflight-chimera7-eco-analog-5-8g-1-6w-vtx-6s-long-range-bnf-elrs-2-4ghz-rx)\n• **Price:** $453.99 (BNF Analog)\n• **Mass:** 660g\n• **Wheelbase:** 327mm\n• **Motors:** XING-E 2809 1250KV\n• **FC:** BLITZ ATF435 / **ESC:** BLITZ E55S 55A\n• **Flight Time:** ~30 min (21700 6S2P 8000mAh)\n• **Prop:** 7.5x3.7x3\n• **Key differentiator:** Same proven Chimera platform at lowest cost ($454 BNF)\n\n**4. SpeedyBee Mario Fold 8 DC** (8\" foldable)\n\n• **URL:** [https://www.speedybee.com/speedybee-mario-fold-8-dc-long-range-drone/](https://www.speedybee.com/speedybee-mario-fold-8-dc-long-range-drone/)\n• **Price:** $339 (Power Kit) – $559 (O3 Kit)\n• **Mass:** 695g (O3 Kit)\n• **Wheelbase:** 360mm (foldable)\n• **Motors:** User-selectable (kit includes motor options)\n• **FC/ESC:** Included in kit\n• **Prop:** 7-8\" compatible\n• **Key differentiator:** Foldable frame (70% volume reduction), 7mm arms, unique mid-size between 7\" and 8\"\n\n**5. iFlight Nazgul XL10 V6** (10\") — _size boundary_\n\n• **URL:** [https://pyrodrone.com/products/iflight-nazgul-xl10-v6-6s-analog-10-inch-long-range-drone-2-5w-vtx-tbs-crossfire-nano-rx](https://pyrodrone.com/products/iflight-nazgul-xl10-v6-6s-analog-10-inch-long-range-drone-2-5w-vtx-tbs-crossfire-nano-rx)\n• **Price:** $759.99 (BNF Analog)\n• **Mass:** 860g\n• **Wheelbase:** 420mm\n• **Motors:** XING2 3314 900KV\n• **FC:** BLITZ F722 / **ESC:** BLITZ E55 55A\n• **Flight Time:** ~40 min hover (21700 6S2P 8000mAh)\n• **Prop:** 10x4.5x3\n• **Key differentiator:** Massive payload capacity for larger/stacked thermal payloads; 10\" may be too large for your target, but included for comparison\n\n───\n\nQuick notes:\n\n• **Flywoo** doesn't make a 7\" — their Explorer LR tops out at 4\"\n• **HGLRC Rekon7** I'd want to dig for a better flight time source since their own product page doesn't","timestamp":1782650993333}}
