{"type":"message","id":"83da906d","parentId":"78aa7825","timestamp":"2026-06-28T12:51:19.505Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, I have most of the data I need. Let me also check the Chimera7 Eco more carefully since we already have AF8a/8b (Chimera7 Pro V2) and AF3a/3b (Chimera9 ECO) in the file. The Chimera7 Eco is a new distinct model.\n\nLet me also look up the HGLRC Rekon7 PRO product page more carefully for the analog variant weight and details.\n\nFor SpeedyBee Mario Fold 8 DC, the O3 Kit is 695g, but there's no specific FC/ESC/motor info beyond the motors being SpeedyBee 2807 1050KV. Let me grab the spec page.\n\nLet me now structure the 5 new candidates:\n\n1. **AF11** - HGLRC Rekon7 PRO (7\")\n2. **AF12** - iFlight SH CineLR 7 (7.5\")\n3. **AF13** - iFlight Chimera7 Eco (7.5\") \n4. **AF14** - SpeedyBee Mario Fold 8 DC (8\")\n5. **AF15** - iFlight Nazgul XL10 V6 (10\")\n\nWait, the data from David says \"5+ New Airframe Candidates\" and he mentions 5. Let me include all 5. Actually I should verify - the Chimera7 Eco is a different model from the Chimera7 Pro V2 (AF8a/8b). And the Chimera9 ECO (AF3a/3b) is a 9\" frame. So the Chimera7 Eco is a 7.5\" budget variant that's distinct.\n\nFor the XL10 - it's 10\". That's bigger than our usual range (7-9\"). David noted \"may be too large\" but included for comparison. I'll add it as a bonus candidate.\n\nLet me now look at what data I need for each:\n\n**AF11 - HGLRC Rekon7 PRO (7\")**\n- URL: hglrc.com product page\n- PNP variant weight: 576g (DJI O3 version without receiver)\n- Wheelbase: 324mm\n- Motors: SPECTER 2806.5 1350KV\n- FC: SPECTER F405 V2\n- ESC: SPECTER 60A BL_S\n- Flight time: ~20-25 min (Alibaba listing, not manufacturer)\n- Battery rec: LiPo 6S 3000mAh / VTC6 2P 4000mAh\n- Prop: HQProp DP7X4X3 7\"\n- GPS: M80 PRO pre-installed\n- For the analog variant, I should look at what the analog version weighs vs the O3 version.\n\nLet me check the analog version weight from the HGLRC page - the page says \"DJI O3 576g( without receiver)\" which suggests the O3 variant. Let me look at the page title which says \"Rekon7 PRO Long Range FPV Analog\" - so this is the analog variant page but the weight is listed for the O3 variant.\n\nActually, I need to be careful here. The page I fetched was titled \"Rekon7 PRO Long Range FPV Analog\" but the specs mention DJI O3. Let me look for the analog variant weight.\n\nFrom the data David provided:\n- Price: ~$549.99 (BNF, analog); ~$599 (HD)\n- Mass: 576g (DJI O3 version)\n\nFor the analog variant, the weight would be less since the analog VTX/cam is lighter than the O3 air unit. The HGLRC SPECTER 60A ESC is 4-in-1.\n\nLet me note this as an estimate. The analog VTX (ZEUS1.6W) + analog cam is probably ~30g lighter than the DJI O3 Air Unit (~44g), so analog variant ~546g. But I should just note what's available.\n\nActually, looking at the page more carefully:\n- It has M80 PRO GPS pre-installed\n- ZEUS1.6W VTX available (analog)\n- Also VISTA HD / DJI O3 Air Unit options\n- Comes with TBS Crossfire Diversity Nano RX pre-installed (\"Optional\")\n\nThe 576g weight is specifically for DJI O3 version without receiver.\n\nFor the analog variant with ZEUS VTX, I'll estimate the weight.\n\nLet me also look at whether this comes as PNP or BNF primarily. The page mentions \"TBS Crossfire Diversity Nano RX pre-installed\" which suggests BNF, but also says \"Receiver（Optional）\". So it could be either.\n\nFrom David's notes: \"Price: ~$549.99 (BNF, analog); ~$599 (HD)\"\n\nLet me now figure out how I want to model this. I'll add AF11 for a BNF analog variant.\n\nFor the Chimera7 Eco - wait, David said the Chimera7 Eco is a different model from what we already have. Let me check what we already have:\n- AF8a: iFlight Chimera7 Pro V2, PNP, 705g, $439.99\n- AF8b: iFlight Chimera7 Pro V2, BNF, 711g, $465.51\n\nThe Chimera7 Eco is:\n- Same 327mm wheelbase as Pro V2\n- XING-E 2809 1250KV (vs XING2 2809 1250KV on Pro V2)\n- BLITZ ATF435 FC (vs BLITZ F722 on Pro V2)\n- BLITZ E55S 55A ESC (vs BLITZ E55 55A on Pro V2)\n- Weight: 660g vs 705g for Pro V2 PNP\n- Price: $453.99 BNF (vs $465.51 BNF for Pro V2)\n- Same 30 min hover with 21700 6S2P\n\nSo it's a budget variant of the Chimera7 platform. Worth adding since it's $12 cheaper and 51g lighter than the Pro V2, with slightly lower-spec electronics.\n\nNow, the SH CineLR 7:\n- 334mm wheelbase\n- XING2 2809 1250KV\n- BLITZ F722 FC / BLITZ E55 55A ESC\n- 770g (without battery)\n- $1,019.99 BNF with DJI O4 Pro - VERY expensive\n- 25 min flight time with 6S 8000mAh Li-ion\n- Key differentiator: no props in view\n\nFor SpeedyBee Mario Fold 8:\n- The OEM version comes with SpeedyBee 2807 1050KV motors\n- 695g (O3 Kit)\n- 360mm wheelbase (foldable)\n- The power kit is $339, O3 kit is $559\n- From David's data: \"7-8\" compatible\"\n\nFor Nazgul XL10 V6 (10\"):\n- Confirmed: 860g, 420mm, XING2 3314 900KV, BLITZ F722, E55 55A, $759.99 BNF Analog\n- 40 min hover with 21700 6S2P 8000mAh\n- GPS included\n\nOK, now I need to define the `maxThrustPerMotor_g` values for each. Let me estimate:\n\n1. HGLRC Rekon7 PRO - SPECTER 2806.5 1350KV on 7\" - ~2.0-2.2 kg per motor (similar to GEPRC 2806.5)\n2. SH CineLR 7 - XING2 2809 1250KV on 7.5\" - same as Chimera7 Pro V2 ~2.0 kg\n3. Chimera7 Eco - XING-E 2809 1250KV on 7.5\" - same ~2.0 kg\n4. Mario Fold 8 - SpeedyBee 2807 1050KV on 8\" - estimate ~2.2-2.5 kg\n5. XL10 V6 - XING2 3314 900KV on 10\" - estimate ~3.5 kg\n\nActually, for the Mario Fold 8 DC, it has two front arms and two rear arms at different lengths (DC = Dead Cat configuration with 360mm front/305mm rear/272mm). The motors are 2807 1050KV. The prop size is \"7-8 Inch\".\n\nFor maxThrust on the HGLRC Rekon7 PRO with SPECTER 2806.5 1350KV - according to GEPRC's SPEEDX2 2806.5 1350KV data which we already have as ~2.7 kg. HGLRC should be similar.\n\nLet me also check if the Chimera7 Eco is PNP/BNF availability. From David's data: $453.99 (BNF Analog).\n\nLet me now decide on the IDs. We already have AF1 through AF10. Let me add:\n- AF11a / AF11b: HGLRC Rekon7 PRO (Analog / HD variants)\n- AF12: iFlight SH CineLR 7 O4 (BNF only, $1020 is high)\n- AF13: iFlight Chimera7 Eco Analog\n- AF14: SpeedyBee Mario Fold 8 DC (Power Kit or O3 Kit)\n- AF15: iFlight Nazgul XL10 V6 Analog (bonus, 10\")\n\nActually, for the SH CineLR 7 at $1,019.99, that's a lot. And for the Nazgul XL10 at 10\" it's a stretch. Let me include both since David included them in his list.\n\nLet me draft all 5 and add them after AF10's closing `}`.\n\nActually, let me think about what variants to create. For HGLRC Rekon7 PRO, I should probably create one variant since the analog/HD versions just differ in VTX/camera. For SH CineLR 7, it's BNF only with O4 Pro. For Chimera7 Eco, BNF analog. For Mario Fold 8, the O3 Kit. For Nazgul XL10, BNF analog.\n\nLet me now write the code. I'll add the 5 new candidates right before the closing `}` of the AirframeCandidates package (after AF10).\n\nLet me check what line numbers I need.\n\nFrom my earlier check, AF10 ends around line 505 with the closing `}` of its part, then line 506 has `}` closing the package.\n\nLet me now compose the insert and add it.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_details"},{"type":"text","text":"Now let me grab the HGLRC Rekon7 PRO spec page for the analog variant weight details"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_7a9798f55aa04c769e9d35af","name":"web_search","arguments":{"query":"HGLRC Rekon7 PRO analog weight grams without battery","count":5},"partialArgs":"{\"query\": \"HGLRC Rekon7 PRO analog weight grams without battery\", \"count\": 5}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":1668,"output":2390,"cacheRead":57088,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoningTokens":2298,"totalTokens":61146,"cost":{"input":0.0001668,"output":0.00047799999999999996,"cacheRead":0.0011417600000000001,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00178656}