{"type":"message","id":"ba709e5b","parentId":"6a5c2386","timestamp":"2026-06-28T12:51:38.529Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great, I now have good data for all 5 candidates. Let me compose them as SysML v2 part usages in the AirframeCandidates package, to be inserted right after AF10 (before the closing of the package and the ThermalCameraCandidates section).\n\nLet me organize the data for each:\n\n**1. HGLRC Rekon7 PRO** (AF11a / AF11b)\n- Analog: 464.3g (without RX) — but this has an F722 FC, 48A ESC, SPECTER 2806.5 1350KV motors\n- DJI O3: 576g (without RX) — same frame, but O3 air unit\n- Wheelbase: 324mm\n- Price: Analog ~$380-430, HD $500-600\n- FC: Zeus F722 / or SPECTER F405 V2 (depending on generation)\n- ESC: Zeus 48A BL_S / SPECTER 60A\n- Motors: SPECTER 2806.5 1350KV\n- Prop: HQProp DP7X4X3 7\"\n- GPS: M80 PRO\n- Flight Time: ~20-25 min (Alibaba) — no official claim\n- Battery: LiPo 6S 3000mAh / VTC6 2P 4000mAh\n\nActually, looking at the HGLRC product page I fetched earlier, it says:\n- FC: SPECTER F405 V2 \n- MCU: STM32F405\n- Gyro: MPU6000\n- ESC: SPECTER 60A 4in1\n- VTX: ZEUS 1.6W VTX / VISTA HD / DJI O3 Air Unit\n- Motor: SPECTER 2806.5-1350KV\n- GPS: M80 PRO\n- Weight: DJI O3 576g (without receiver)\n\nBut from rcdrone.top: analog version weighs 464.3g with Zeus F722 + Zeus 48A ESC.\n\nSo there are different hardware variants. I'll create two: AF11a for the analog version, AF11b for the DJI O3 version.\n\n**2. iFlight SH CineLR 7** (AF12)\n- Frame: H-shaped, 334mm wheelbase\n- FC: BLITZ F722\n- ESC: BLITZ E55 4-IN-1 2-6S 55A\n- VTX: DJI O4 Air Unit Pro (integrated)\n- Motors: XING2 2809 1250KV\n- Prop: HQ 7.5X3.7X3\n- Weight: 770±5g (Without Battery)\n- Flight Time: Up to 25 min (slow cruising)\n- Battery: 6S 4000mAh Li-ion above or 6S 3300mAh LiPo\n- Price: $1,019.99 BNF (very expensive)\n\n**3. iFlight Chimera7 Eco** (AF13)\n- Wheelbase: 327mm\n- FC: BLITZ ATF435\n- ESC: BLITZ E55S 4-IN-1 55A\n- VTX: BLITZ Whoop 1.6W VTX\n- Motors: XING-E 2809 1250KV\n- Prop: 7.5X3.7X3\n- Weight: 660g (Without Battery)\n- Flight Time: ~30 min (21700 6S2P 8000mAh)\n- Price: $453.99 BNF Analog\n\n**4. SpeedyBee Mario Fold 8 DC** (AF14)\n- Foldable frame, 360mm wheelbase\n- 7mm arms, 7-8\" props\n- Weight: 695g (O3 Kit)\n- Motors: SpeedyBee 2807 1050KV (Power Kit) or user-selectable\n- FC/ESC: Included in kit\n- Price: $339 (Power Kit) - $559 (O3 Kit)\n- No props in view design (folding)\n\nWait, looking at the specs more carefully:\n- The Mario Fold 8 DC comes as a kit, not a pre-built BNF/PNP\n- Power Kit ($339): frame + stack (FC/ESC) + motors + props\n- O3 Kit ($559): same + DJI O3 Air Unit\n- Weight: 695g (O3 Kit) — this is the complete kit weight\n\nActually the specs page mentions:\n- Product Name: SpeedyBee Mario Fold 8 DC Long Range Drone\n- Wheelbase: DC FOLD:360mm Front:305mm Rear:272mm\n- Weight: 695g (O3 Kit)\n- Motors: SpeedyBee 2807 1050KV Motor (included in kit)\n- Propellers: 7-8 inch\n\nBut there's no FC/ESC details beyond \"SpeedyBee 35A AIO\" mentioned elsewhere. This is more of a DIY kit. Let me model it as-is.\n\nActually, looking at the notes: \"FC mounting hole: 30.5x30.5(M3) & 20x20mm (M3)\" and \"Internal installation height: 22-31mm\"\n\nLet me model it as much as I can with available data and note gaps.\n\n**5. iFlight Nazgul XL10 V6** (AF15)\n- 10\", 420mm wheelbase\n- FC: BLITZ F722\n- ESC: BLITZ E55 4-IN-1 55A\n- VTX: BLITZ Whoop 1.6W/2.5W VTX\n- Motors: XING2 3314 900KV\n- Prop: HQ 10X4.5X3\n- Weight: 860g (Without Battery)\n- Flight Time: ~40 min hover (21700 6S2P 8000mAh no load)\n- Price: $759.99 BNF Analog\n- GPS: Pre-installed (GPS+SBAS+Galileo+QZSS+Glonass)\n- Receiver: TBS Crossfire Nano RX\n\nNow let me format all of these as SysML v2 part usages.\n\nActually, I realize the Nazgul XL10 V6 may not have receiveProtocols and uartCount listed from the page. I can infer from the F722.\n\nLet me create the entries and add them after AF10's closing brace.\n\nI need to be careful about the formatting. Let me write the content to insert after line 505 (the `}` closing the AirframeCandidates package). Actually looking at the file structure:\n\nLine 479: part AF10 : Airframe {\nLine 504: `:>> manufacturerFlightTimeBattery = \"6S 3300mAh LiPo\";`\nLine 505: `  }`\nLine 506: ` }`\nLine 507: (blank)\nLine 508: ` // =========================================================================`\nLine 509: ` // THERMAL CAMERA CANDIDATES  ...`\nLine 510: ` // =========================================================================`\nLine 511: ` package ThermalCameraCandidates {`\n\nSo I need to insert after AF10 } and before the closing } of the AirframeCandidates package, and before the ThermalCameraCandidates section.\n\nActually wait, look at lines 505-506:\n```\n505:   }        // closes part AF10\n506:  }         // closes package AirframeCandidates? \n```\n\nWait, the indentation is confusing. Let me look again.\n\nLooking at the structure:\n- `package AirframeCandidates {` opens\n- Each `part AFxx : Airframe {` ... `}` opens and closes\n- `}` closes the package\n\nLine 505 closes AF10. Line 506 must close the package. Then line 507 blank, line 508 ThermalCameraCandidates.\n\nSo the closing of the AirframeCandidates package is at line 506. I need to insert the new candidates BEFORE line 505 (the closing `}` of AF10), or better yet, BETWEEN AF10's closing `}` and the package's closing `}`.\n\nActually looking more carefully:\nLine 505: `  }`  (closes part AF10, 2-space indent)\nLine 506: ` }`   (closes package AirframeCandidates, 1-space indent)\nLine 507: blank\nLine 508: ` // =========================================================================`\nLine 509: ` // THERMAL CAMERA CANDIDATES`\n\nSo I need to insert new candidates between lines 505 and 506. I'll add them after the `  }` that closes AF10 but before the ` }` that closes the package.\n\nLet me compose the 5 new parts and insert them.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_details"},{"type":"text","text":"Now I have good data. Let me compose and insert all 5 airframe candidates into `candidates.sysml`, right after AF10 and before the package closes.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_30a02640f827475da59638d0","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/candidates.sysml","offset":502,"limit":10},"partialArgs":"{\"path\": \"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/candidates.sysml\", \"offset\": 502, \"limit\": 10}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":2028,"output":2014,"cacheRead":58624,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoningTokens":1880,"totalTokens":62666,"cost":{"input":0.0002028,"output":0.0004028,"cacheRead":0.00117248,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00177808}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1782651080546,"responseId":"gen-1782651081-8FOPL4T2p3KVNNEtt6vS"}}
