{"type":"message","id":"22344fc7","parentId":"3a439d52","timestamp":"2026-06-29T01:38:53.560Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user asked \"Remind me what SPC have we selected for this drone build?\" - SPC stands for Single Point Crossover, but in this context it might mean something different. Let me think about this in the context of our thermal surveillance drone project.\n\nActually, looking at the model, we have:\n- Requirements (R1-R8)\n- CameraRequirements\n- Component definitions in Architecture\n\nBut the user is asking about \"SPC\" - this could be a trade study abbreviation. Let me search our memory files and the model for anything related to SPC.\n\nActually, in systems engineering, SPC could stand for \"System Performance Characteristic\" or \"System Performance Criteria\" or could be a specific trade study acronym. Let me check memory and handoff files for context.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_details"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_4081550baa6743cfbbb2eaae","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone && grep -rni 'SPC' memory/ 2>/dev/null; grep -rni 'SPC' session-handoffs/ 2>/dev/null"},"partialArgs":"{\"command\": \"cd /home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone && grep -rni 'SPC' memory/ 2>/dev/null; grep -rni 'SPC' session-handoffs/ 2>/dev/null\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":343,"output":257,"cacheRead":67584,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoningTokens":159,"totalTokens":68184,"cost":{"input":0.0000343,"output":0.000051399999999999996,"cacheRead":0.00135168,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00143738}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1782697125453,"responseId":"gen-1782697127-kizkAgCo1yPxqaQSL0dw"}}
